2026-05-27 11:37:36 -04:00: Done. Here's the summary:
2026-05-27 11:37:36 -04:00: 
2026-05-27 11:37:36 -04:00: **Root cause:** `/api/live-signals` had a 3-tier staleness fallback — journal → Firebase. At audit time (15:30 UTC), Firebase timed out (4s limit), so the route fell through to the stale journal (May 11, 382h old). Minutes later Firebase recovered and the endpoint started returning a fresh timestamp (15:05 UTC, 31 min old).
2026-05-27 11:37:36 -04:00: 
2026-05-27 11:37:36 -04:00: **Fix applied** (`src/app/api/live-signals/route.ts`):
2026-05-27 11:37:36 -04:00: - Added `desk_pipeline.sqlite` `cycle_metadata.completed_at` as a **secondary fallback** between the stale journal and the Firebase network call
2026-05-27 11:37:36 -04:00: - New fallback chain: journal → desk pipeline (local SQLite, no network) → Firebase
2026-05-27 11:37:36 -04:00: - This means a Firebase outage now degrades to "20h stale" (last desk cycle) instead of "382h stale" (dead journal)
2026-05-27 11:37:36 -04:00: 
2026-05-27 11:37:36 -04:00: **Current state:** `lastCycleTime` = 31 min ago, health `ok: true`, Discord notified.
